{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "52ed4f56-6200-8c59-8938-61641319a13f",
  "created_at": "2026-01-05T11:26:47-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Ileana Quintero",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:24:58-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Lorraine. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:25:02-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, good morning. My name is Ileana Quintero. I am calling because my recycling bin was left at the curb with a tag on it, and the tag says rejected. No way, I put out the same things as always."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:25:14-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, Mrs. Quintero, I'm sorry about that. Can I get the address where the bin is?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:25:19-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Three eighty-four Dixon Street. In the North End."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:25:22-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Three eighty-four Dixon Street. Got it. And do you know what the tag said, besides rejected? Was there a reason checked off?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:25:29-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me see, I have it here, I brought it inside. [pause] It says contamination, and then a little box about plastic bags. Maybe is the bags, I put the papers in a bag to keep them dry. Is that not allowed?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:25:41-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's usually the issue, yes. Recyclables generally need to go in loose, not bagged. So you'd want to take the papers out of the bag and put them in the bin by themselves."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:25:51-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, okay, okay. Loose, no bags. I can do that. So I take the tag off and just put it out again?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:25:58-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, fix it and put it out for your next pickup. They won't come back today for it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:26:04-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, of course. So when is the next pickup? I never remember, it changes with the holidays."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:26:10-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me look at your street. Dixon Street, North End. [pause] Your recycling is the next scheduled week, so Monday, a week from today, and the holiday shifts are done now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:26:19-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A week from today, Monday. Okay. Thank you. And one more thing, my neighbor has so many wind chimes, wicked loud, I could not sleep with the wind. But that is not for you, no?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:26:30-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That one's not Public Works, I'm afraid. You'd want to check with the city about noise complaints, I can transfer you if you'd like."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:26:38-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, no, it's fine. Thank you very much."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:26:41-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. So bagless, out next Monday. Take care, Mrs. Quintero."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T11:26:45-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Bye bye."
    }
  ],
